# promise: #476
# Chrome closes the hidden Browser that holds a profile's pages and, with its last Chrome window gone, unloaded
# the profile while Cra's pages still used it: Chrome's check that a profile's pages close before it does stopped
# Cra (~WebContentsOfBrowserContext from ProfileDestroyer::Timeout, two 0.1.44 crash reports). Cra turns
# DestroyProfileOnBrowserClose off, so its profiles stay loaded until it quits (bridge.mm). Default never unloads
# (Cra's DevTools pipe keeps it), so the page is on the space Random, on the profile Hobbies (as in
# new-document-command). On an engine without the change it stops in ~WebContentsOfBrowserContext, as the reports
# did (checked 17 Nov; an `arg` can't turn the feature back on: the bridge's --disable-features wins).
budget rss=700
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false, "newDocumentApps": {"Default": "googleDoc"}}
